            <div xml:id="d1413">

                <pb facs="1139" n="1129" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg1129"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.9531/6–3049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Tsingtao</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hawthorne</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tsingtao</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-30T10:00:00+08:00">June 30, 1949—10
                            a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:16 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>302. Chinese military yesterday began removing from compound at 1 Kwangsi Road
                    Consulate General’s stocks of gas, kerosene and luboil (remytel 281, June
                    21).</p>
                <p>Sent Department 302, repeated Nanking 210, Shanghai 126.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hawthorne</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
